            <ArticleTitle>[The current significance of spinal cord stimulation in the framework of functional neurosurgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1025-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal cord stimulation (DCS) has proved effective in different types of Deafferentation Pain. Long-term results are good in 60-85% of cases. DCS improves microcirculation and ischemia in cases of inoperable peripheral vascular diseases. Advantages of this method are: Absence of severe complications and estimation of the effect during the test phase. - Nevertheless, other neurosurgical possibilities (destructive pain surgery, spinal/cerebral application of medicaments) continue to preserve their indications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
